      "body": "The JSON-LD data-model comparator (object key order insignificant; array order significant only inside `@list`) is now copy-pasted into at least three test binaries: `crates/sparq-jsonld/tests/flatten.rs`, `crates/sparq-jsonld/tests/round_trip.rs`, and the `sparq-conformance` `jsonld_suite/common.rs` lane helper (plus a fourth variant in `crates/sparq-jsonld/examples/jsonld_conformance.rs`). Rust integration tests are separate binaries so there is no free sharing, but the duplication is a real drift hazard: the conformance ratchet floors are measured with one copy while the crate-local acceptance tests use another, and a fix to one copy's semantics (e.g. the numeric/`Json::Raw` guard) silently does not reach the others.\n\nSuggested fix: hoist the comparator to a `#[cfg(feature = \"test-util\")]` (or `pub mod testing`) surface in `sparq-jsonld` so every consumer links the SAME implementation, then delete the copies. Needs a decision on whether that surface is public API or an opt-in dev-only feature \u2014 hence not done inline.\n\n> \ud83e\udd16 Discovered by the SPARQ worker while implementing #3210. Out-of-scope for that PR; captured as follow-up.\n<!-- sparq-followup:v1 -->",
